<<<
There are certain verb groups about which the question is conceivable— Should they be allowed to be interrupted by adverbs? Such are the infinitive e.g. to try (may we say to earnestly iry?), the compound verb e.g. have thought (may we say I have never thought so?),
===
There are certain verb groups about which the question is conceivable—Should they be allowed to be interrupted by adverbs? Such are the infinitive e.g. *to try* (may we say *to earnestly try*?), the compound verb e.g. *have thought* (may we say *I have never thought so*?),
>>>

<<<
the copula & complement e.g. was a riddle (may we say He was in some ways a riddle?), the verb & its object e.g. passed the time (may we say It passed pleasantly the time?),
===
the copula & complement e.g. *was a riddle* (may we say *He was in some ways a riddle*?), the verb & its object e.g. *passed the time* (may we say *It passed pleasantly the time*?),
>>>

<<<
the gerund & its governing preposition e.g. by going (may we say by often going?).
===
the gerund & its governing preposition e.g. *by going* (may we say *by often going*?).
>>>

